 ### [EnvMap-GS](18915-envmap-gs.md)
-Separates foreground and background, constraining background primitives to a spherical shell and baking them into an environment map [18915-envmap-gs.md].
+EnvMap-GS is a two-stage Gaussian Splatting framework designed to reconstruct outdoor "inside-out" captures where a camera moves within a restricted navigation area while looking outward at a distant environment. It explicitly separates foreground and background regions to eliminate "floaters" (large, erroneous Gaussians in the far field) caused by incorrect initialization and limited view ranges. Unlike standard 3D Gaussian Splatting, which struggles with far-field reconstruction, EnvMap-GS constrains background primitives to a spherical shell and allows the background to be baked into an environment map for faster rendering.
 
 ### [Thermal-Physics-Informed 3D Gaussian Splatting](18935-thermal-physics-informed-3d-gaussian-splatting.md)
-Embeds infrared radiative transfer modeling (Planck’s law) into Gaussians for physically interpretable thermal representation [18935-thermal-physics-informed-3d-gaussian-splatting.md].
