 ### [MAC-Splat](19210-mac-splat.md)
-Enforces direct 3D consistency supervision using semantically informed 2D correspondences for sparse-view reconstruction [19210-mac-splat.md].
+MAC-Splat is a training framework for sparse-view 3D Gaussian Splatting that resolves depth and correspondence ambiguities by enforcing direct 3D consistency supervision. Unlike methods relying on 2D photometric losses or proxy geometry, it uses semantically informed 2D correspondences to anchor and jointly regularize the position, shape, and appearance of matched Gaussians in a shared world coordinate frame.
 
 ### [Heat Kernel Textures (HKTex)](19427-heat-kernel-textures-hktex.md)
-Uses anisotropic heat kernels as geodesic equivalents to Gaussians on manifold surfaces, eliminating UV mapping artifacts [19427-heat-kernel-textures-hktex.md].
+Heat Kernel Textures (HKTex) is an intrinsic, UV-free texture representation that uses anisotropic heat kernels as geodesic equivalents to Gaussians, defined directly on any manifold surface discretized as a triangular mesh. It solves the problems of UV mapping—such as seams, distortions, wasted memory, and vertex duplication—by operating natively on the manifold rather than in ambient Euclidean space. Unlike standard 3D Gaussian Splatting, which detaches from geometry, HKTex kernels bend to conform to the surface, and unlike UV mapping, it eliminates artifacts by construction.
 
 ### [Gaussian Splatting in Style](19431-gaussian-splatting-in-style.md)
