 ### [Sketch and Patch](20108-sketch-and-patch.md)
-Categorizes Gaussians into Sketch (boundaries/high-frequency) and Patch (smooth/broad) roles for specialized encoding [20108-sketch-and-patch.md].
+Sketch and Patch is a hybrid 3D Gaussian representation method that categorizes Gaussians into two distinct roles: **Sketch Gaussians**, which define scene boundaries and high-frequency features, and **Patch Gaussians**, which cover smoother, broader regions. It solves the problem of storage inefficiency and redundancy in standard 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS), where adaptive density control overestimates densification needs in high-frequency areas, leading to redundant Gaussian clusters along edges. Unlike conventional 3D downsampling or tiling which degrade visual quality due to the tightly coupled, heterogeneous nature of 3DGS Gaussians, this method separates Gaussians by role to allow specialized encoding.
 
