 ### [Laplacian Frequency Hierarchies](20304-laplacian-frequency-hierarchies.md)
-Decomposes image supervision into low/high-frequency components, training separate fields and archiving lower-frequency fields to reduce active count [20304-laplacian-frequency-hierarchies.md].
+Laplacian Frequency Hierarchies is a training optimization method for 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) that decomposes the image supervision signal into low-frequency and high-frequency components, training separate Gaussian fields for each component in a coarse-to-fine sequence. Unlike prior frequency-based methods that use frequency cues only for scheduling or resolution adjustment, this method incorporates frequency at the representation level by factorizing the scene into frequency-specific fields and archiving completed lower-frequency fields to reduce the active Gaussian count during subsequent high-frequency optimization. It serves as a plug-and-play module that reduces training time and peak memory usage while maintaining competitive reconstruction quality, particularly at high resolutions.
 
 ### [Gradient-Aware Super Sampling (GASS)](20492-gradient-aware-super-sampling-gass.md)
-Extracts image gradients to guide a refinement network for high-fidelity super sampling from low-resolution inputs [20492-gradient-aware-super-sampling-gass.md].
