 ### [DeltaSplat](20851-deltasplat.md)
-Iterative refinement module for pose-free feed-forward 3DGS, conditioning per-Gaussian updates on per-pixel Plücker rays and rendered depth [20851-deltasplat.md].
+DeltaSplat is a lightweight, iterative refinement module for pose-free feed-forward 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) that corrects geometric and photometric errors introduced by single-pass prediction and camera estimation uncertainty. It distinguishes itself from prior residual refinement methods like [DeSplat](12925-desplat.md) by conditioning per-Gaussian updates on per-pixel Plücker rays and rendered depth, providing a soft geometric prior that disambiguates 2D rendering residuals into reliable 3D corrections under uncalibrated or predicted camera poses.
 
 ### [Rendering Implementation and Acceleration](21069-rendering-implementation-and-acceleration.md)
-Defines the computational pipeline for projecting and alpha-blending Gaussians via tiling, sorting, and culling [21069-rendering-implementation-and-acceleration.md].
